# Grouped cloud detail refinement

## Applied result

The existing `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/Maps/L_RXSkySystem_CloudCards` now uses `M_RXGroupedCloud_Detail` for all eight grouped planes. Actor placement, source VDB layout, sky brightness, and the earlier daytime whiteout overrides are preserved. CloudDome remains invisible on the copied RX actor.

New material-instance controls in the English `Cloud Detail` category have Korean tooltips:

| Parameter | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| CoreDepthStrength | 0.65 | Reduce ambient and multiple-scattering fill in dense shadowed regions; preserve direct transport. |
| DetailReliefStrength | 0.5 | Reinforce measured sharp-versus-broad transport differences using existing texture samples; no synthetic noise. |
| EdgeFeatherWidth | 0.08 | Narrow the low-coverage fade (previously 0.12) to retain wisps. |

The parent is `/Game/RXSkySystem/CloudCards/Study03Grouped/Materials/M_RXGroupedCloud_Detail`. It is a separate asset; the previous parent remains available.

## WestTower resolution pilot

Only `RX_Grouped_WestTower` received the new two-texture 2048-square bake. Its material is `/Game/RXSkySystem/CloudCards/Study03DetailPilotV2/WestTower/Materials/MI_WestTower_Detail`. The other seven groups retain their 1024 textures and now use the shared detail shader. The previous grouped package manifest describes the initial bake; this document records the active variant.

The pilot retains slots 8,3,17,19 and the original projection. Source DetailMip was capped at 1.0 in the isolated bake collection only. Four off-axis 1024 tiles produce each 2048 pass; eleven directions/coverage passes each accumulate eight actual samples per tile (352 captures). Resolution and mip changes were evaluated together, so the observed improvement cannot be attributed to resolution alone. This is not a higher-resolution reconstruction of the underlying VDB.

Positive RGB: local +X/+Y at 20 degrees, +Z. Positive A: separately rendered coverage. Negative RGB: local -X/-Y at 20 degrees, -Z. Negative A: mean horizontal transport. Both textures are linear HDR with alpha preserved. Native scene-capture alpha is not cloud coverage.

The earlier `Study03DetailPilot` attempt has incomplete black capture assets after a hidden-renderer check failed. They are not used by the final cards. Valid output is `Study03DetailPilotV2`; do not use the unsuffixed pilot as a bake source.

## Review and limits

Evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXCloudDetailPilot`. Same-camera captures include `before_1k.png`, `texture_2k.png`, and `detail_2k.png`. Reviewed 10.0, 17.8, 22.0 and the eastern view. Restored time 15.36 and left the preview looking west so the pilot is visible. The source bake renderer/material, lighting, active state and capture quality settings were restored successfully.

The reviewed daylight silhouette and internal shading improved without visible tile seams. Sunset backlighting still flattens the large mass, and nighttime contrast remains subtle; those are not claimed solved. Fixed-view planes still lack volumetric parallax and inter-group dynamic shadows. No frame-time or GPU-memory benchmark was performed; only the representative group's texture resolution increased.

Native material compilation passed with zero errors. Recursive audit checked 33 material/mesh dependency packages with no MCP, VDB, or CloudAuthoring dependency. The full offline profile passed 42/42; the 1,839-file frozen candidate check reported no changed inputs afterward. Runtime packaging was not tested. Offline verification evidence and frozen hashes are stored beside the captures.
